  "reasoning": "According to records from the Congressional Research Service and historical appropriations data, the last time Congress enacted all regular annual spending/appropriations bills before the start of the fiscal year (October 1) was for Fiscal Year 1997 (completed in late September 1996). In every year since Fiscal Year 1998 (beginning in 1997), Congress has failed to pass all regular appropriations bills before the October 1 deadline, relying instead on stopgap continuing resolutions and omnibus packages enacted well past the start of the fiscal year.",
